<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rises in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate rose in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	27.37	    +  8	    27.27     27.41</p>
<p>91-Day	26.85	    + 28	    26.53     26.99</p>
<p>182-Day     25.62	    - 14	    25.44     25.72</p>
<p>350-Day     25.68				25.14     25.99</p>
<p>Last week the 358-day paper was assigned at 25.59 pct.</p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   3.366 bln pesos     3.74</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.579 bln pesos     3.98</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   3.272 bln pesos     3.64</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   1.651 bln pesos     2.75</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.60 compared with 3.45 the week before, on demand of 11.39 billion pesos the week before.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   4  basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			  14  basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			 10  basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			 31  basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
</text>
